# Family Values (AtroUI)

Inspired by [Family Values](https://benji.org/family-values). We **do** use Family Values — these three philosophies are how we practice it in UI, UX, and animation. Table-stakes (utility, performance, security, a11y, `prefers-reduced-motion`) are never traded away.

## 1. Simplicity through gradual revelation

Show the fundamental first. Reveal depth only when it is relevant.

- Fundamentals stay visible; options appear in context (overlay / tray / step), not all at once.
- One primary action or idea per focused surface (tray, dialog step, hero signature).
- Prefer progressive disclosure over dumping every control on screen.
- Keep place: overlay on the current task rather than full-screen teleport mid-flow.
- Opinionated defaults — ship the good version; don’t ask the user to configure the basics.

## 2. Fluidity through seamless transition

Motion clarifies path A→B (space, direction, cause). Elements travel; they don’t teleport.

- Shared elements that persist should **morph / travel**, not remount as duplicates.
- Prefer short tweens (`easeOutExpo`-ish) over spring overshoot for chrome (drawers, menus) — overshoot feels glitchy on web.
- Directional motion for hierarchical nav; lateral / fade for peer switches.
- Fixed overlays: portal to `document.body`, iOS-safe scroll lock (`apps/docs/hooks/use-body-scroll-lock.ts`), shared easings (`apps/docs/lib/motion.ts`).
- Never animate “for vibes” without an architectural reason (continuity, hierarchy, or cause).

## 3. Careful delight

Polish everywhere; sprinkle magic selectively. Delight is earned, not constant fireworks.

- Frequent paths: tiny details only (copy feedback, caret blink, label morph).
- Rare paths: stronger moments only when earned (install complete, first success).
- Corners count (empty states, errors, 404) — dirty bathroom problem.
- Avoid AI-slop atmosphere: no soft blur-orb soup as identity. Prefer intentional material (owned sketch voice, deferred WebGL underpainting, quiet chrome).
- Soft-rect via `--radius` by default — not capsule CTAs everywhere.

## When editing UI

1. Name which Family Values principle you’re serving.
2. Prefer shared motion tokens over one-off springs.
3. Respect reduced motion: skip decorative motion; keep clarity.
4. Mobile is first-class — no “CSS bloom only” excuses that leave a lifeless frame.
